#: ../../../env_vars.rst:2
msgid "Environment variables"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../env_vars.rst:6
msgid "How Poe the Poet uses environment variables"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../env_vars.rst:8
msgid ""
"Poe tasks inherit environment variables from the host shell, but tasks also "
"run with additional variables that are provided via the following channels, "
"ordered with ascending precedence. The principle for precedence is that "
"variables closer to the task override those further away."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../env_vars.rst:10
msgid "Host environment variables (what poe receives as ``os.environ``)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../env_vars.rst:11
msgid ""
"Project level :ref:`env files<Loading external environment variables>` (in "
"the order listed)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../env_vars.rst:12
msgid "Project level :ref:`env config<Global environment variables>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../env_vars.rst:13
msgid "Parent task variables"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../env_vars.rst:14
msgid "Task level :ref:`env files<envfile_option>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../env_vars.rst:15
msgid ""
"Task level :ref:`env config<Setting task specific environment variables>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../env_vars.rst:16
msgid ""
"Output values from tasks configured as dependencies via the :doc:"
"`uses<guides/composition_guide>` option"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../env_vars.rst:17
msgid "Variables set by task :doc:`args<guides/args_guide>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../env_vars.rst:19
msgid ""
"As well as being exposed to the task at runtime, environment variables can "
"also be templated into some other task configuration fields."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../env_vars.rst:21
msgid ""
"For ``cmd`` tasks expansion of variables via bash parameter expansion syntax "
"is performed as part of resolving the command to run as a subprocess."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../env_vars.rst:24
msgid "Private variables"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../env_vars.rst:26
msgid ""
"Variables that start with ``_`` and contain no uppercase characters are "
"treated as private, which means that they're available for use in "
"configuration time (which includes parameter expansion within ``cmd`` "
"tasks), but are not exposed to the task subprocess at runtime. This applies "
"to all variables set via project or task level configuration."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../env_vars.rst:28
msgid ""
"It is a good practice to use private variable names for ``args`` or ``uses`` "
"unless you specifically want those values to be set on the task environment."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../env_vars.rst:30
msgid ""
"In the following example, the ``_food`` arg will cause the task to accept an "
"option like ``--food sausages``, and will be accessible as a variable in the "
"task config, but not as an environment variable at runtime."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../env_vars.rst:32
msgid ""
"[tool.poe.tasks.cook]\n"
"script = \"kitchen:frying_pan(_food)\"\n"
"args = [{ name = \"_food\", default = \"eggs\" }]"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../env_vars.rst:40
msgid "Variables managed by Poe the Poet"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../env_vars.rst:43
msgid "Internal Environment variables"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../env_vars.rst:45
msgid ""
"The following environment variables are used by Poe the Poet internally, and "
"can be accessed from within configuration and tasks."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../env_vars.rst:47
msgid ""
"``POE_ROOT``: path to the parent directory of the main tasks file (e.g. "
"pyproject.toml)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../env_vars.rst:48
msgid ""
"``POE_PWD``: the current working directory of the poe process (unless "
"overridden programmatically)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../env_vars.rst:49
msgid ""
"``POE_CONF_DIR``: the path to the parent directory of the config file that "
"defines the running task or the :ref:`cwd option<Setting a working directory "
"for included tasks>` set when including that config."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../env_vars.rst:50
msgid ""
"``POE_ACTIVE``: identifies the active PoeExecutor, so that Poe the Poet can "
"tell when it is running recursively."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../env_vars.rst:51
msgid ""
"``POE_VERBOSITY``: reflects the current verbosity level. Normally 0 is the "
"default, 1 means more verbose and -1 means less."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../env_vars.rst:54
msgid "Special variables"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../env_vars.rst:56
msgid ""
"The following variables are not set on the environment by default but can be "
"referenced from task configuration as if they were."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../env_vars.rst:58
msgid ""
"``POE_GIT_DIR``: path of the git repo that the project is part of. This "
"allows a project in a subdirectory of a monorepo to reference :ref:"
"`includes<Including files relative to the git repo>`, :ref:`envfiles<Loading "
"environment variables from an env file>`, or :ref:`virtualenv "
"location<Configure the executor for a task>` relative to the root of the git "
"repo. Note that referencing this variable causes poe to attempt to call the "
"``git`` executable which must be available on the path."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../env_vars.rst:60
msgid ""
"``POE_GIT_ROOT``: just like ``POE_GIT_DIR`` except that if the project is in "
"a git submodule, then the path will point to the working directory of the "
"main repo above it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../env_vars.rst:63
msgid "External Environment variables"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../env_vars.rst:65
msgid ""
"The following environment variables can be set to modify Poe the Poet's "
"behavior."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../env_vars.rst:67
msgid ""
"``POE_PROJECT_DIR``: used as the default value for the ``--directory`` "
"global argument."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../env_vars.rst:68
msgid ""
"``NO_COLOR``: disables ansi colors in output (unless the ``--ansi`` argument "
"is provided)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../env_vars.rst:69
msgid ""
"``FORCE_COLOR``: forces ansi colors in output when set to a non-zero value "
"(overridden by ``NO_COLOR`` or the ``--no-ansi`` argument)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../env_vars.rst:70
msgid ""
"``POE_DEBUG``: can be set to ``1`` to enable printing debug messages to "
"stdout."
msgstr ""
